    "Both halves are industrious, and that shared work ethic is the strongest bond between them. The pull in different directions comes from freedom. Capricorn accepts long commitments as the price of achievement, while the Horse bolts when it feels confined, so this person may commit eagerly and then chafe. Understood as complexity, that tension makes them good at work that combines a fixed destination with flexible methods, such as freelance projects, field roles or new ventures. Negotiating autonomy explicitly before accepting responsibilities works better than resenting them later. Consider breaking long goals into short sprints with real breaks between them, which satisfies the Horse's need for fresh starts while keeping Capricorn's ladder in sight.",
